{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 d5 4. exd5 Qxd5 5. Nc3 Qd8 6. d4 { Authored anchor. Nc3 develops while attacking the queen. After her retreat White has gained time, but still needs to complete development and address f4. } 6... Bd6 7. Bc4 Bf5 8. O-O Nc6 9. Nb5 Nge7 10. Nh4 Be6 { Plan: Bring out the bishops, castle and keep the central pawns supported. The extra developing tempo should become piece activity rather than premature queen moves. Opponent resource: A queen chased once is not trapped. Black can catch up if White spends several moves trying to hunt it. } *

