{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 d5 4. exd5 Nf6 5. Bb5+ c6 6. dxc6 Nxc6 { Authored anchor. The checking bishop invites ...c6, after which exchanges accelerate Black's development too. This optional branch teaches why a check is not necessarily a gain of time. } 7. Nc3 Bd6 8. Qe2+ Be6 9. Ng5 O-O 10. Nxe6 Qa5 { Plan: Withdraw the bishop safely when attacked and establish d4 if the position permits. Compare activity and king safety before claiming a material gain. Opponent resource: Black's knights have natural central squares and open lines. Taking more pawns can leave White behind in development. } *

