{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. e5 Nh5 5. d4 d6 { Authored anchor. e5 attacks the knight, which heads to h5 to help preserve f4. Black challenges the advanced e-pawn with ...d6. } 6. Qe2 d5 7. Nc3 Nc6 8. Bd2 Bf5 9. O-O-O Qd7 10. Qf2 g6 { Plan: Develop Bc4 or Bd3 as appropriate and examine exd6 only after considering the recapture. White must maintain central support while the knight is offside. Opponent resource: The h5 knight still influences f4 and g3. Do not push g4 without calculating ...fxg3 en passant when legal and the effect on king safety. } *

