{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 Be7 4. Bc4 Bh4+ 5. Kf1 { Authored anchor. The bishop reaches h4 with check along the diagonal to e1. Kf1 answers it without pushing more kingside pawns, but permanently gives up castling. } 5... c6 6. Nc3 b5 7. Bb3 a5 8. a3 Be7 9. d4 a4 10. Ba2 d5 { Plan: Develop d4, Nc3 and the queen bishop while finding a safe place for the king. Treat rook coordination as a task; castling is no longer available. Opponent resource: Black can open the center with ...d5. Do not continue a routine castling plan after the king has moved. } *

