{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 Be7 4. Bc4 Nf6 5. e5 Ng4 { Authored anchor. White gains space with e5 and Black places the knight actively. The g4 knight can create threats against e5 or f2; its location is more important than a general developing rule. } 6. O-O O-O 7. d4 d5 8. Bb3 Ne3 9. Bxe3 fxe3 10. Nc3 Be6 { Plan: Use d4 and careful development. Before castling, check the tactical relation between the knight, the f-pawn deficit and the bishop on c4. Opponent resource: Bxf7+ is not automatically sound. Black's king may survive while your pieces lack support. } *

