{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. d4 d5 5. exd5 Qxd5 6. Nc3 { Authored anchor. Black develops and then hits the center. Nc3 gains a queen tempo, but the exchanges also release Black's pieces. } 6... Bb4 7. Bd3 Qe6+ 8. Kf2 Nge7 9. Bxf4 Qd7 10. a3 Bd6 { Plan: Complete development and compare queen retreats before choosing a bishop square. A broad center is useful only while it remains defended. Opponent resource: Black can answer a threat with a check or a capture. Verify the queen's active squares before assuming a free attack. } *

