{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 e5 2. f4 Bc5 3. Nf3 d6 4. c3 Nf6 5. d4 exd4 6. cxd4 Bb6 7. Nc3 { Authored anchor. White uses c3 to support d4 while the bishop keeps pressure on the king side. Exchanging in the center gives White space but opens lines. } 7... Nc6 8. e5 Nd7 9. d5 Ne7 10. Bd3 Nc5 { Plan: Develop the bishops, castle and keep the d4-e4 center defended. Chase the bishop only when it improves the position, not just because it is visible. Opponent resource: The c5-b6 bishop watches the sensitive f2 square. Capturing e5 at the wrong time may permit ...Qh4+ and a king attack. } *

