{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 e5 2. f4 Bc5 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. Nc3 d6 5. Bc4 Nf6 6. d3 { Authored anchor. Both sides develop naturally. White keeps the option of a later f-pawn exchange without forcing an immediate central confrontation. } 6... a5 7. fxe5 dxe5 8. Bg5 h6 9. Bh4 Be6 10. Qe2 O-O { Plan: Castle, identify whether d4 is achievable and improve the least active piece. A quiet maneuvering game is a normal outcome of a gambit being declined. Opponent resource: Black can use ...Bg4 to pin Nf3 or open the center. Do not weaken the king with repeated pawn moves while pieces remain at home. } *

