{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 e5 2. f4 d5 3. exd5 e4 4. d3 Nf6 5. dxe4 Nxe4 6. Nf3 { Authored anchor. Black ignores the offered f-pawn and builds an advanced e4 wedge. d3 challenges it directly; exchanges change the position into a development battle. } 6... c6 7. Be3 cxd5 8. Bb5+ Nc6 9. O-O Be7 10. Ne5 Qd6 { Plan: Develop the bishops and castle. Attack the central knight with useful moves only after checking tactics along the e-file. Opponent resource: Black's development can be rapid and the king remains on e1. A greedy attempt to keep every extra pawn can allow a central attack. } *

