{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 e5 2. f4 d5 3. exd5 c6 4. Nc3 exf4 5. Nf3 { Authored anchor. White declines to spend another tempo taking a wing pawn and develops. Black sacrifices or returns material to obtain central and diagonal activity. } 5... Be7 6. Bc4 Nf6 7. dxc6 Nxc6 8. d4 O-O 9. Bxf4 Bg4 10. Be3 Qb6 { Plan: Stabilize the d-pawn if it is useful, otherwise let material return for development. Check the c-file and queen routes after any dxc6 capture. Opponent resource: Capturing c6 blindly can give Black easy development with ...Nxc6. The point is the resulting activity, not the label countergambit. } *

