{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. Be2 O-O 6. O-O { Authored anchor. White takes the center and develops normally against a fianchetto. This bridge does not require sacrificing the f-pawn or launching an immediate attack. } 6... e5 7. dxe5 dxe5 8. Nxe5 Nxe4 9. Nxe4 Qxd1 10. Rxd1 Bxe5 { Plan: Complete development and support e4 before choosing d5 or a kingside expansion. Black's ...c5 and ...e5 are the breaks to monitor. Opponent resource: A large center can become a target. The g7 bishop becomes active when central pawns exchange. } *

